<article id="post-88797" class="post-88797 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-birmingham tag-bar tag-birmingham tag-chez-fonfon tag-dining-2 tag-frank-stitt tag-frankie tag-image tag-meal tag-menu tag-pardis-stitt tag-picture tag-restaurant tag-review tag-wine-list">
	<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title">Chez Fonfon, Birmingham, 3/17/23</h1>
		<div class="entry-meta">
						<span class="posted-on"><a href="https://diningwithfrankie.com/2023/04/16/chez-fonfon-birmingham-3-17-23/" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date published" datetime="2023-04-16T09:37:38-05:00">April 16, 2023</time><time class="updated" datetime="2023-03-23T16:37:51-05:00">March 23, 2023</time></a></span><span class="byline"><span class="sep"> ~ </span><span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://diningwithfrankie.com/author/hsnixon/">hsnixon</a></span></span>					</div><!-- .entry-meta -->
	</header><!-- .entry-header -->

	<div class="entry-content">
		<figure id="attachment_88996" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-88996" style="width: 656px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img data-recalc-dims="1" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-attachment-id="88996" data-permalink="https://diningwithfrankie.com/2023/04/16/chez-fonfon-birmingham-3-17-23/img_5919-2/" data-orig-file="https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5919.jpeg?fit=4032%2C3024&amp;ssl=1" data-orig-size="4032,3024" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;1.78&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;iPhone 14 Pro Max&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;1679080314&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;6.86&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;800&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0.033333333333333&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}" data-image-title="IMG_5919" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="&lt;p&gt;exterior&lt;/p&gt;
" data-large-file="https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5919.jpeg?fit=656%2C492&amp;ssl=1" class="size-large wp-image-88996" src="https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5919.jpeg?resize=656%2C492&#038;ssl=1" alt="" width="656" height="492" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5919.jpeg?resize=1024%2C768&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5919.jpeg?resize=300%2C225&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5919.jpeg?resize=150%2C113&amp;ssl=1 150w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5919.jpeg?resize=768%2C576&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5919.jpeg?resize=1536%2C1152&amp;ssl=1 1536w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5919.jpeg?resize=2048%2C1536&amp;ssl=1 2048w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5919.jpeg?resize=1200%2C900&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5919.jpeg?resize=800%2C600&amp;ssl=1 800w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5919.jpeg?resize=400%2C300&amp;ssl=1 400w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5919.jpeg?resize=200%2C150&amp;ssl=1 200w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5919.jpeg?w=1312&amp;ssl=1 1312w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5919.jpeg?w=1968&amp;ssl=1 1968w" sizes="(max-width: 656px) 100vw, 656px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-88996" class="wp-caption-text">exterior &#8211; <strong>2007 11th Ave. S, Birmingham, AL, 35205</strong></figcaption></figure>
<p>Chez Fonfon was a casual French bistro that opened in 2000.  It is under the helm of Chef Frank Stitt but the night we were there it was his wife Pardis Stitt who was on site.  (She also is a co-owner of Highlands Bar and Grill).  The large place was crowded and busy with a large bar taking up about a third of the room.  Music was in the background, lights were lowered, windows looked out to the street and parking, and the good-sized tables were bare wood set with cloth napkins.  The vibe was of younger people and lively conversations.   We were lucky to get a table in a corner, otherwise, the noise might have made me like the place less. Service was good as was the food, which was first-rate.  I&#8217;d go back, especially for the dessert.<span id="more-88797"></span></p>
