<p>&nbsp;</p>
<h3>Food</h3>
<p>We started with one of their drinks, a pecan old-fashioned.  It was made with bourbon, pecan orgeat and angostura.   Most importantly it was not sweet but the overall taste didn&#8217;t make me think of pecans.  It was just a well-made old-fashioned with a little twist.</p>
<figure id="attachment_89001" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-89001" style="width: 656px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img data-recalc-dims="1" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-attachment-id="89001" data-permalink="https://diningwithfrankie.com/2023/04/16/chez-fonfon-birmingham-3-17-23/img_5947-5/" data-orig-file="https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5947.jpeg?fit=4032%2C3024&amp;ssl=1" data-orig-size="4032,3024" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;2.2&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;iPhone 14 Pro Max&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;1679080890&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;2.22&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;1600&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0.033333333333333&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}" data-image-title="IMG_5947" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="&lt;p&gt;Frankie enjoyed a cocktail&lt;/p&gt;
" data-large-file="https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5947.jpeg?fit=656%2C492&amp;ssl=1" class="size-large wp-image-89001" src="https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5947.jpeg?resize=656%2C492&#038;ssl=1" alt="" width="656" height="492" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5947.jpeg?resize=1024%2C768&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5947.jpeg?resize=300%2C225&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5947.jpeg?resize=150%2C113&amp;ssl=1 150w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5947.jpeg?resize=768%2C576&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5947.jpeg?resize=1536%2C1152&amp;ssl=1 1536w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5947.jpeg?resize=2048%2C1536&amp;ssl=1 2048w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5947.jpeg?resize=1200%2C900&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5947.jpeg?resize=800%2C600&amp;ssl=1 800w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5947.jpeg?resize=400%2C300&amp;ssl=1 400w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5947.jpeg?resize=200%2C150&amp;ssl=1 200w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5947.jpeg?w=1312&amp;ssl=1 1312w, https://i0.wp.com/diningwithfrankie.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/IMG_5947.jpeg?w=1968&amp;ssl=1 1968w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 656px) 100vw, 656px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-89001" class="wp-caption-text">Frankie enjoyed a pecan old-fashioned cocktail</figcaption></figure>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The Salade Fonfon had a farm egg with walnuts, blue cheese and dijon vinaigrette.  The egg quarters were cooked to a fudgy yolk.  The mix of greens was mostly Romaine and it was underdressed.  We ordered it wanting to have something green with the meal and then had to substitute asparagus on the dinner plate for the salad that came with the steak.  A more experienced server would have mentioned this earlier, but it was his first day.  Anyway, the walnuts added a nice crunch to the greens but the blue was a mild variety.   It was good, not great.</p>
